{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Pashua and kachash.</b> Verb forms, and pashua is in the pa'ul pattern." "<b>Vanusog.</b> A verb form from the nif'al pattern, like ve-nishloach (Esther 3:13)." "<b>Sarah.</b> From the root of sorer umoreh (Deuteronomy 21:18)." "<b>Horu like asu (Job 40:13).</b> And horu is from the root of al birkat hori (Genesis 49:26), ve-tahar et Miriam (1 Chronicles 4:17), and it is on the pattern of huggu, and the vav reverts to the root. Some say it should have been on the pattern of banah baniti (1 Kings 8:18), but a shift occurred." "The meaning of <b>milev:</b> from their heart they utter words of falsehood."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {3 "Reading ובאו זרות as referring to an anomalous shift in pattern; the phrase is elliptic and translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:20.523587781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}